  "notes": "AAT Level 2 Certificate in Accounting (Q2022, 603/6338/1), qualification specification version 5.7, September 2026. Four mandatory units: Introduction to Bookkeeping 25% of the grade, Principles of Bookkeeping Controls 25%, Principles of Costing 20% (each a 1 hour 30 minute computer-marked unit assessment), The Business Environment 30% (assessed only in the 2 hour synoptic assessment, partly human marked). Per 50-question test: ITBK 13, POBC 12, PCTN 10, BENV 15. Within units the counts follow the learning outcome weightings (ITBK five LOs at 20% each, POBC four at 25%, PCTN 30/40/20/10, BENV by the synoptic assessment objectives). Pools are exactly 4x per-test counts. Only knowledge that fits a four-option item is modelled: entering transactions into ledgers, spreadsheet tasks and the synoptic's written responses are not.",
